Let Project settings scroll on a phone.

The dialog had no height cap, and its fields stack on a narrow screen, so on
a phone it's taller than the screen: centred on it, its description and its
Save and Cancel buttons sit off the top and bottom, and the Dialog's
scroll-lock keeps the page from scrolling to them. A sandbox project's
Repositories field makes it taller still.

The dialog is now capped at 85% of the viewport, as upstream's Add agent
dialog is, and the form scrolls between the header and the Save and Cancel
buttons, which move out of it and submit it by its id. A dialog that fits,
as on a desktop, is unchanged.

Upstream bug: delete once upstream's ProjectSettingsDialog
(web/src/shell/ProjectSettingsDialog.tsx) caps its height and scrolls its
fields.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0041.

